# Agent split (this portfolio)

**Claude Code** (terminal / recruiting-season agents): better at UI/UX, visual design, and writing. Prefer handing those surfaces to Claude.

**This Cursor agent:** owns everything else end-to-end — APIs, scan/pipeline, git, deploy, data models, War Room wiring, Claude integration plumbing, bugfixes that are not primarily copy/design.

## When the user asks for copy, design, or UI polish

1. Do **not** freestyle long marketing copy, page redesigns, or visual redesigns yourself if Claude is available for that lane.
2. Implement structure/plumbing here if needed, then give a **pasteable brief** for Claude Code (goal, files, constraints, acceptance bar).
3. Wire Claude’s output into the app after they produce it (imports, routes, deploy).

## Claude Code’s lane (examples)

- Page / section copy, tone, headlines, story Bank polish
- Prep briefs, comparison *memo* language, outreach drafts
- CSS/layout/visual hierarchy refinements, landing polish, War Room visual polish
- Design-system-feeling UI iteration

## This agent’s lane (examples)

- `/api/*`, Gmail/Calendar/Drive/scan, pipeline JSON, GitHub commits
- Auth, env, Vercel, CI, type-safe joins (`companyId`, comparison schema)
- Canvas sync from JSON when asked; keep Claude Code off `.canvas.tsx` unless user says otherwise
- Comparison scores *schema* and War Room table wiring (Claude may refresh scored *writing* via `agents/compare.md`)

## Claude writing style (prep, debriefs, living notes)

Gold standard: the Brain Co Google Doc
(`https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qqrwcstj98k0L9e67vPpiwCcDA3kdvHUEtXOssBRW2o`).

- Real title + section titles that name the conversation or theme
- Short hyphen bullets and readable prose judgment ("How to read this…")
- Interview line to reuse + Action items
- No markdown tables, no em dashes
- Do not dump raw `##` into Drive as plain text. Sync via HTML headings (`markdownToDriveHtml`)
- Prefer human notes in `data/debriefs/*` over auto stubs when they exist
- Auto-prep lives in `lib/recruiting/prep-llm.ts` and should mirror Brain Co, not a consulting deck

## Default handoff line to Claude Code

```text
Cursor owns infra. You own writing + UI/UX/design for this task.
Constraints: [files / don’t touch]. Writing: Brain Co Google Doc living-notes style (real titles, readable sections, no em dashes, no tables). Deliver: [artifacts]. Stay out of API keys, deploy, and pipeline wiring unless asked.
```
